- # PhD Research Companion for Computer Science 🔬
- A comprehensive end-to-end research lifecycle management system designed for computer science doctoral students conducting systematic, reproducible academic research with full traceability and compliance requirements.
- > **"Scientific research is an iterative art – every great paper undergoes 5-8 rounds of destruction and reconstruction."**
- ## 🎯 Why This Skill Exists
- ### The Problem:
- PhD students in computer science face numerous challenges:
- - ❌ Literature scattered across arXiv, DBLP, ACM Digital Library, IEEE Xplore – no unified view
- - ❌ Research directions change frequently based on advisor feedback – easy to lose track
- - ❌ 6-8 rounds of paper revisions with version chaos and lost changes
- - ❌ Incomplete experiment logs make reproducibility impossible (10+ years later)
- - ❌ Missing "留痕" (traceability) documentation fails audit requirements by national research agencies
- - ❌ No systematic approach to validate mathematical consistency, logical soundness
- ### Our Solution:
- ✅ **Automated multi-source literature review** with technical thread identification
- ✅ **Advisor meeting tracking** with structured action items
- ✅ **Version-controlled paper writing** (LaTeX + Git) with 6-8 iteration support
- ✅ **Rigorous experiment design & execution** with automatic logging
- ✅ **Mathematical consistency validation** before submission
- ✅ **Complete scientific traceability system** (留痕管理) for audit compliance
- ✅ **Top-tier journal preparation workflow** (IEEE TIFS, ACM TOIS, NeurIPS, etc.)
- ## 📊 Research Workflow Overview
- Phase 0: Direction Selection → Phase 1: Literature Survey → Phase 2: Advisor Alignment →
- Phase 3: Writing & Experiment Design → Phase 4: Iterative Revision (6-8 Rounds) →
- Phase 5: Submission & Publishing
